WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.115 --> 00:00:02.640
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.160
- All right, so there
are two new things about

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.573
this new laptop from Apple.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.086
The new color and the new chip.

00:00:10.086 --> 00:00:12.840
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.220
Everything that was already great about

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:17.790
the outside of Apple's laptop
redesign is still great.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:18.900
It still has a bunch of ports.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.300
The full size HDMI, the
MagSafe is still here,

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.386
still has that high quality
build, the boxy design,

00:00:24.386 --> 00:00:26.250
the super bright display.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.750
Also everything that was awkward about it

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.160
is also still awkward about it.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.550
Still has this nice big notch
at the top with just a webcam

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:33.660
and no face unlock.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.590
But it comes in black now, kind of.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.680
It looked a lot darker in
Apple's announcement video.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.530
Like the color is literally
called Space Black, right?

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.291
So I'm expecting a really,
really black laptop.

00:00:46.291 --> 00:00:48.270
And in the commercial it looks awesome.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.610
They talk about this fancy
new anodization process

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.920
for the aluminum, so it's not a coating,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.560
it's an actual new chemistry
process that is a part

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.300
of the anodization itself.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.400
It's supposed to be extra
fingerprint resistant.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.185
But now that we actually
have it here, in reality,

00:01:02.185 --> 00:01:05.381
I mean, it's darker, but like,

00:01:05.381 --> 00:01:08.100
it's just a little bit darker

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.130
than the other Space Gray from before.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.570
If you wanna see a black laptop,

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.460
this is a black laptop,

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.530
like they make black laptops already.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:19.830
So Apple's here is just,
it's a darker gray.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.450
I think it's basically the darkest

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:25.230
that Apple could get without
showing a ton of fingerprints.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.210
I mean, it still does show
some fingerprints a little bit.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.490
It's definitely not completely immune.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.980
But compared to some other
black laptops I've tried,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.150
it is better than those.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.360
So it's somewhere in the middle
of not so many fingerprints,

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.199
but also darker than normal.

00:01:38.199 --> 00:01:41.640
It's fine, it's darker, which is nice.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.160
Like some camera angles it
hits, it really looks dark,

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.170
but you get the idea.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.003
It also, if you're curious,

00:01:47.003 --> 00:01:48.690
it also comes with black apple stickers,

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:51.450
and it also comes with a
black MagSafe charging cable,

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.820
but also, that braided cable
is darker than the end.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.450
And it also comes with a
brick that's still white.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.010
So I wouldn't say they fully committed

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:01.170
to the Space Black theme quite yet.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.000
I'll give 'em partial credit.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.910
But then let's talk about the chip inside.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.520
So the new three nanometer M3 family

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.720
of chips gets announced

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.010
and it does offer some

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.830
nice improvements over
the M2 family, definitely.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.390
It almost feels weird to compare it

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.550
to the M2 stuff because almost nobody

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.010
with an M2 should be upgrading to this,

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.630
but at least it's a
good frame of reference.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.180
So I've been testing
the absolute highest end

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:26.310
M3 Max in this laptop,

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:28.890
which from the M2 Max
goes from a 38 core GPU

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.780
to a 40 core GPU.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:35.780
And from 96 gigs of shared
memory to now up to 128 gigs.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:39.090
CPU wise, Apple's claims were about right.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.390
Somewhere in the 20 sometimes
30% improvement range

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.310
over last year, which is very respectable.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:46.770
And actually, it's a bigger
jump in single core performance

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.020
than I was expecting, which is awesome for

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.060
just the daily use, the quick snappy,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.700
everyday computing, browsing type stuff.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.510
And then GPU wise, this is
where more people were hoping

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.010
for a little bit of a bigger improvement.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:01.530
And again, it is a respectable bump.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.560
Not quite leapfrogging
the big discreet GPUs,

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:08.250
but still putting M3
Max's GPU up at the level

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.200
of M1 Ultra.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.130
So that's pretty impressive.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.660
And matching somewhere

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.930
around AMD Radeon RX 6800 on benchmarks

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:19.200
or about an RTX 3070, which is, you know,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.090
we're talking a fairly
mid-range card at this point.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.120
But that's the thing about
all this new GPU performance

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.620
and the benchmarks and all that is great,

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.290
but what's actually more
interesting, at least to me,

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.260
is what you're actually going to do with

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:34.043
that extra performance,
that extra graphics power.

00:03:34.043 --> 00:03:38.310
And for a laptop like this,
that's typically games

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:41.730
or high powered graphics
related applications.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.910
So yeah, when you see that
powerful new GPU in a laptop

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:47.250
with new hardware accelerated ray tracing

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:50.400
for the first time in a
Mac and the mesh shading

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.240
and all that, probably the
first thing you think is gaming.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.430
But then you realize it's a Mac.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:59.280
So probably not gaming.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.200
But really I think the
reason, at least in my head,

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.560
that most people don't
associate gaming with Macs

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.270
is not because they're not powerful.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.920
I mean, they're not as powerful

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.860
as the highest industry
GPUs, but they're not bad.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.350
It's just because the
games that people play

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:15.150
and are enthusiastic about

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.090
are often not available on the Mac.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.440
Like, I'm not even a big PC gamer,

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.230
but you already know, if you
want to play "The Witcher,"

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:25.507
the new "Fallout," "Skyrim," "Crysis,"

00:04:25.507 --> 00:04:27.690
"Apex Legends," there's a long list.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:30.660
And if you want to throw
maximum GPU power at that game

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.300
to play it in the best possible quality,

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.720
you're looking to optimize
a PC, not buy a Mac.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.490
So I actually think, and
I think it's maybe worth

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:39.420
an entire separate video,

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:40.560
maybe let me know if you're interested,

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.770
but I think gaming on
the Mac is in an all time

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:45.810
interesting place right now,

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:47.700
because again, lots of games
are not available on the Mac,

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.580
but this is the most powerful
Mac that's ever been made.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.110
And I've been playing
with some of the games

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:54.360
that Apple likes to show
off, like in the app store.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.880
They're like, "Guys, we have games.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.920
There's lots of games
and they're really good

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.170
and they take advantage of the new stuff."

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:03.810
I've been playing this
game called "Lies of P."

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.340
It's one of the ones they
talked about in the keynote

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.173
and it takes advantage

00:05:06.173 --> 00:05:07.740
of the hardware accelerated ray tracing.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.410
You can see it in the
reflections and on the floor

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.150
and in the sword and everything.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:15.270
It plays amazing. Like it looks great.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:18.660
Frame rates stay high. I'm
playing at 4K resolution.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:23.070
There's a visual depth and
detail that's beautiful.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:26.340
Plus, macOS Sonoma has the gaming mode,

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.640
which is allocating as much
power as possible to this game.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.350
It also lets you use
a Bluetooth controller

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.870
with way faster sampling
and lower latency.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:38.040
And so just maxing out
everything works great.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.960
It's an awesome playing experience.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.550
I was very impressed.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:45.540
I just don't care about this game.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:48.690
I'm not invested in that
particular game at all.

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:50.040
It was fun to play the demo,

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.740
and I was impressed with the
actual moment of the computing.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.170
It would get a little warm
and the fans would spin up,

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:56.160
but the fact that it would work

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.870
on those Mac settings is amazing.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.640
I just don't, I'm not
invested in that game at all.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:02.040
And I think that sort of
encapsulates the way I feel

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.930
about all this extra GPU power,

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.801
is like, you could use it for gaming,

00:06:05.801 --> 00:06:08.970
but if you're gonna buy a
computer for this much money

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.190
to game, you're not buying a Mac.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:14.790
But then again, of course,
this is a Pro laptop,

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:15.623
it's a MacBook Pro.

00:06:15.623 --> 00:06:18.180
And so there are lots of other
non-games that take advantage

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.830
of this extra GPU power

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.170
and of this new hardware
accelerated ray tracing

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:23.700
and the mesh shading and all of that.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:26.340
Things like Cinema 4D and this laptop

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:29.460
with this chip is better than
ever at all that stuff too.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.020
And I think we're actually
gonna slowly start seeing

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.910
even more apps on the Mac take advantage

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.650
of this stuff as time goes on.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:38.850
But my conclusion was, okay,
look, when the event happened,

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:41.340
I watched it and that
last video you can see in

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.470
that hotel room, and I
was very excited about it.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.600
It got announced, I saw
a new matte black MacBook

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:47.550
with a new chip, and I thought that

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:51.390
that new color on top of that new chip

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.730
would be enough for me to go,
"All right, you know what?

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:56.010
It's finally time, I'm gonna upgrade."

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:58.590
So I did, I clicked the order button

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:01.560
and I purchased a new maxed out

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:04.380
M3 Max MacBook Pro in matte black.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.270
But now that I've actually
had this review unit here,

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:08.880
and I've gone through my
testing and I've experienced it,

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.610
the color is kind of nice,

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.830
but it's not quite as impressive

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.960
and new as I was maybe hoping.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.210
And then the new chip,
it's great and everything,

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:20.220
but it's not actually going

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:22.980
to make a meaningful
difference to my workflow.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.950
With a couple of videos I
edit on the go on my laptop

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:29.193
from the M1 Max laptop
that I've been using.

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:32.490
So I canceled.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.590
I logged in and I canceled my order

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:38.760
and I will continue to daily
what I have for the past,

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:40.350
I guess, three years now,

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.720
with the M1 Max 16 inch MacBook Pro.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:43.770
Turns out it's not for me.

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.020
Well, I mean, I guess it is a
high-end matte black laptop.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.220
So maybe it is kind of for me.

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:48.270
But I think the point I'm trying

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:52.770
to make is if you already
have an M family chip MacBook

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:54.930
in the tier that you want,

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.570
meaning if you have an
M2 Pro or an M1 Pro,

00:07:57.570 --> 00:07:59.880
M3 Pro is not gonna be the
huge difference for you.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:02.880
If you have M2 Max or M1 Max,

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:05.520
M3 Max is not really for you.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:08.040
This is like any other spec bump

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:10.590
far more for people with older machines.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:11.730
You didn't need to hear me say this,

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.410
but it's true for people
with older machines,

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.030
with Intel machines,

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.220
or with machines in a different tier,

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.620
where this would really
unlock something new

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.300
in their workflow.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.200
And that's what's great about 'em,

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.390
is you're gonna get a
better machine than ever.

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:26.160
For me, I'm gonna keep using M1 Max.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:28.620
That's a testament to
how good that thing is.

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:30.570
Maybe I'll do a two years later,

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.580
three years later review
or something like that.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:36.600
But for now, I'm glad there's
a new darker color available.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.300
But yeah, you know,
it's weirdly not for me.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:41.340
Still a great laptop,
still great displays,

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.830
amazing speakers, awesome build quality,

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.570
battery life's still awesome.

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:48.000
But maybe my upgrade will come when

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.760
they really commit to
the matte black thing

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:53.643
or there's another huge upgrade
somewhere down the line.

